      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "I AM A ROCKSTAR (1) gets the nod after a fair second-up platform at Leonora, where he was fourth behind Shimari and beaten just over three lengths after working home evenly. The 3kg claim is useful against the top weight and his record at around this distance is solid enough for this field, with three placings from six attempts. GIGI GOGO (5) was also in that Leonora race and was kept safe near the top of an open market before finishing fifth, beaten three and a half lengths, so she has the profile to be closer if she finishes off from a better striking point. TINY CHAMPION (3) brings the most consistent recent finishing pattern, with consecutive thirds and two placings from two tries around 1400m, although her winning edge remains to be proven. GINGERIFFIC (4) was the recent near-miss, second to Racy Rascal at Leonora, and while she rises in weight from that run, another honest effort puts her in the minor-money picture. WILLYABRUP (6) is worth keeping safe.",
